<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n22201" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ĭn-āresco</span></b> ,
			ārui, 3, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>v. inch. n.</i>, <i>to
				become dry in</i> any place, <i>to dry up</i>,
				<i>become quite dry</i> (post-Aug.).
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">in sole,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					26, 8.40, § 66</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">for which: caenum illitum sole,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					31, 6, 32, § 61</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">opus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vitr. 7,
					3</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">medicamenta,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cels.
					5, 17 <i>fin.</i></span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fructus ante maturitatem,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Col.
					4, 24, 3</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">germina multa cum inaruere,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					27, 11, 71, § 95</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nihil facilius quam lacrimas inarescere,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Quint. 6, 1, 27</span></i>
			.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>, <i>to dry up</i>, <i>become exhausted</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ne (liberalitas) nimia profusione inarescat,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					Ep. 2, 4, 4</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
